{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative, coverage-oriented supervisor: random_walk is used for exploration in clear states, move_forward is used in a short commit state, and obstacle events trigger explicit, directed recovery turns. Recovery states only allow a single, safe turn action and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for the rare case of being blocked on all sides. All transitions are deterministic and safe.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to model open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes a compact, deterministic supervisor: random_walk for exploration, move_forward for short progress, explicit turn recovery for obstacles, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
